{"field":"keywords","before":["Elizabeth Holmes enneagram","Elizabeth Holmes type 3","Elizabeth Holmes personality","Elizabeth Holmes 3w2","Achiever enneagram","Theranos founder personality","Elizabeth Holmes voice fake","Liz Holmes rebrand"],"after":["Elizabeth Holmes enneagram","Elizabeth Holmes personality type","Elizabeth Holmes Type 3","Elizabeth Holmes voice","Theranos founder personality","Elizabeth Holmes prison","You Can See Everything Elizabeth Holmes"]}
{"field":"faqs","before":[{"anchor":"what-is-elizabeth-holmess-personality-type","answer":"Elizabeth Holmes is an Enneagram Type 3 (The Achiever), specifically a 3w2. The pattern shows in the age-nine letter to her father announcing she wanted to 'discover something new' (a shape without a subject), the Channing Robertson 'another Bill Gates or Steve Jobs' quote she kept on her desk before building anything, the fabricated baritone voice and Jobs-replica turtleneck, the board of statesmen assembled as social proof, and the 600+ 'I don't know' answers in deposition when the costume failed.","question":"What is Elizabeth Holmes's personality type?"},{"anchor":"what-elizabeth-holmess-voice-was-costuming","answer":"Yes. In a 2023 New York Times interview, Holmes spoke in her natural higher pitch and quietly confirmed the deep voice had been an affectation. Former Theranos employees, including early design lead Ana Arriola and reporter John Carreyrou, had documented her dropping the baritone at company gatherings for years. The voice, the unblinking stare, the bulk-bought Issey Miyake turtleneck — all pieces of a wardrobe, not a person.","question":"Was Elizabeth Holmes faking her deep voice?"},{"anchor":"why-elizabeth-holmes-stayed-with-sunny-balwani-for-a-decade","answer":"Holmes met Sunny Balwani in 2002 when she was 18 and he was 37 and married. He moved into her house, became Theranos COO, and told her she had to 'kill the old Elizabeth' to make it in business. For a Type 3, 'kill the old Elizabeth' is not a threat — it is a job description. She was already wired to become whatever the room required. He was asking her to become more of the only person she knew how to be.","question":"Why did Elizabeth Holmes stay with Sunny Balwani for a decade?"},{"anchor":"what-elizabeth-holmes-does-in-prison","answer":"Holmes is serving her sentence at the federal prison camp in Bryan, Texas, working as a reentry clerk for 31 cents an hour — helping fellow inmates polish their resumes and apply for jobs and benefits. She has begun posting warnings about an imminent AI-driven privacy apocalypse and has filed for clemency. The achievement engine doesn't stop. It just changes costumes.","question":"What is Elizabeth Holmes doing in prison?"}],"after":[{"question":"What is Elizabeth Holmes's personality type?","answer":"This analysis interprets Elizabeth Holmes as an Enneagram Type 3, with moderate confidence, based on her pursuit of recognition as a medical innovator and management of her public identity. The assessment is not a confirmed self-typing or clinical diagnosis; her wing and instinctual subtype remain uncertain.","anchor":"what-is-elizabeth-holmess-personality-type"},{"question":"Was Elizabeth Holmes faking her deep voice?","answer":"Reporting describes differences between Elizabeth Holmes’s conversational and public voices. Amy Chozick’s 2023 profile reported a consciously created business persona. Holmes and Billy Evans later disputed aspects of the profile; the Times stands by it. This evidence cannot settle the origin or intent of every vocal change.","anchor":"what-elizabeth-holmess-voice-can-tell-us"},{"question":"What has Elizabeth Holmes said about Sunny Balwani?","answer":"At her November 2021 trial, Holmes alleged sexual and emotional abuse by her former partner and Theranos executive Sunny Balwani. He denied the allegations. Their separate fraud verdicts do not establish whether jurors accepted particular abuse allegations, and personality type cannot explain why someone remains in an allegedly abusive relationship.","anchor":"why-the-sunny-balwani-relationship-resists-a-simple-explanation"},{"question":"Where is Elizabeth Holmes now, and when could she be released?","answer":"On September 9, 2026, the Bureau of Prisons listed Holmes at Bryan FPC with a projected release date of February 22, 2030, which can change. Her prison term was reduced to 123 months in March 2026. DOJ’s September 1 update listed her 2025 commutation petition as pending.","anchor":"what-elizabeth-holmes-does-in-prison"},{"question":"What is the new Elizabeth Holmes documentary?","answer":"You Can See Everything is directed by Nathan Fielder and Lance Oppenheim. It screened at Telluride on September 6, 2026. A24 says it begins with Holmes inviting a crew into her life 34 days before prison. Its official teaser announces October, while the film page still lists the specific date as to be determined.","anchor":"what-you-can-see-everything-adds"}]}
